\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Design envelopes of Leps-P for a new material tested by a new laboratory, at laboratory specimen size, by rock quality and void ratio: median (thick lines) and 5th percentile (thin lines) of the mean envelope. The shaded zone exceeds the largest normal stress in the database.}}{28}{figure.caption.23}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Out-of-sample evaluation, leaving out each publication: (a) coverage of the 80\% interval by range of normal stress without site tests; and (b) mean CRPS of ln $\tau $ for held-out tests at $\sigma '_n$ $\ge $ 2 MPa with site tests at $\sigma '_n$ $\le $ 1.5 MPa (bars: 95\% bootstrap intervals over publications; filled: recommended procedure).}}{29}{figure.caption.24}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Waste rock of the example: (a) laboratory-scale envelopes by rock type with the site tests (open symbols: tests flagged by the conflict check); and (b) envelopes of placed waste rock (void ratio 0.65, maximum particle size 1 m) by rock type and dump-average envelope. Dotted vertical lines mark the largest normal stress of the site tests.}}{30}{figure.caption.25}%
